# Line endings are load-bearing here, not cosmetic.
#
# web/test/frozen.mjs pins field.html and the eleven files it loads by sha256. Those checksums
# are computed over the bytes on disk, so if a checkout hands one machine CRLF and another LF,
# the first gate in `npm test` fails on every machine except the one that ran `npm run freeze`.
# That is exactly what was happening: four of the twelve frozen files were CRLF in a Windows
# working tree and LF in the repository, so a clean clone anywhere else -- CI, a judge
# reproducing the build -- failed before any test ran.
#
# Pinning eol=lf makes the working tree match the blob on every platform, so the checksums mean
# the same thing everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touch these, on any platform.
*.png   binary
*.gif   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.bin   binary
*.gz    binary
*.pt    binary
*.ipynb binary
